       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "10594239"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Widely expressed with lowest expression in liver and spleen"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "TISSUE SPECIFICITY"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "15940259"
      },
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "19203586"
      }
     ],
     "value": "By p53/TP53; expression is directly activated by TP53. TP53 phosphorylation on 'Ser-15' is required to activate the PHLDA3 promoter"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "INDUCTION"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "value": "The PH domain binds phosphoinositides with a broad specificity. It competes with the PH domain of AKT1 and directly interferes with AKT1 binding to phosphatidylinositol 4,5-bisphosphate (PIP2) and phosphatidylinositol 3,4,5-trisphosphate (PIP3), preventing AKT1 association to membrane lipids and subsequent activation of AKT1 signaling"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "DOMAIN"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "value": "PHLDA3 genomic locus is frequently observed in primary lung cancers, suggesting a role in tumor suppression"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "MISCELLANEOUS"
  },
  {
   "texts": [
    {
     "evidences": [
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Belongs to the PHLDA3 family"
    }
   ],
   "commentType": "SIMILARITY"
  }
 ],
